      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s interesting to see how we all write this; I think I\u0027d land on something like this (untested as well):\n\n```\nfn table_data(font_ref: \u0026BridgeFontRef, tag: u32, offset: usize, data: \u0026mut [u8]) -\u003e usize {    \n    let table_data \u003d font_ref\n        .0\n        .as_ref()\n        .and_then(|f| f.table_data(u32tag_to_tag(tag)))\n        .map(|d| d.as_ref()) \n        .unwrap_or_default();\n\n    // probably best not to take more bytes than we actually have, or more than fit in data\n    let slice_length \u003d std::cmp::min(table_data.len().saturating_sub(offset), data.len());\n\n    if let Some(table_bytes) \u003d table_data.get_mut(offset..offset + slice_length) {\n        // Slice target buffer in case the chunk to be read is smaller than the target\n        // buffer due to a specified offset.\n        data.get_mut(0..slice_length).unwrap().copy_from_slice(table_bytes);\n        slice_length\n    } else {\n        0usize\n    }\n}\n```",
